<title>UK: AIM Global launches sterling money market fund.</title>
<headline>AIM Global launches sterling money market fund.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>AIM Global said in a statement that it had launched a triple-A rated sterling money market fund, the Sterling Portfolio of Short Term Investments Co (Global Series) Plc, an umbrella fund domiciled in Dublin.</p>
<p>Money market funds offer investors an alternative to short term bank deposits and AIM said it expects the concept to catch on in the UK.</p>
<p>In the U.S., $750 billion in cash is managed via money market funds, AIM said. -- David Chance London newsroom 44 171 542 5887</p>
</text>
